; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Lunchbox Lists
; CATEGORY: Lists & Data Structures
; LEVEL:    Beginner
; TAGS:     lists, first, last, fput, lput, butfirst, item, count
; SUMMARY:  Packs and unpacks a lunchbox to show the basic list commands, drawing the list as a row of boxes after every step.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   A list is a row of things in order. The program starts with an
;   empty lunchbox and uses one list command per step: FPUT puts food
;   at the front, LPUT at the back, BUTFIRST and BUTLAST take food
;   off the ends, ITEM peeks at one place. After every step the list
;   is drawn as a row of boxes, one row lower each time, with the
;   command that made it written on the left.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run and read the picture from top to bottom. Each row is
;   the lunchbox after the command written beside it.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * FPUT and LPUT add to the front and the back
;   * BUTFIRST and BUTLAST give the list without one end
;   * FIRST, LAST, ITEM and COUNT look without changing anything
;   * lists are never changed in place: MAKE stores the new one
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Add a step that uses REVERSE.
;   * Use MEMBERP to check whether there is an apple in the box.
;   * What does FIRST of an empty lunchbox do? Try it and read the error.
; ============================================================

make "lunch []
make "row 0

; Draw the list as boxes. CMD is the command text shown on the left.
to drawlunch :cmd
  localmake "y 250 - 62 * :row
  penup setxy -390 :y - 22 setpencolor "purple label :cmd
  localmake "x -50
  if emptyp :lunch [penup setxy :x :y - 22 setpencolor "grey label [empty]]
  foreach :lunch [
    penup setxy :x :y setheading 90 setpencolor "blue pendown
    repeat 2 [fd 100 rt 90 fd 34 rt 90]
    penup setxy :x + 8 :y - 22 setpencolor "black label ?
    make "x :x + 108
  ]
  make "row :row + 1
end

; Run one step: show it, run it, and draw the result. The step is
; given as a list of Logo words so we can both print it and RUN it.
to stepdo :instruction
  run :instruction
  print (sentence :instruction [->] :lunch)
  drawlunch :instruction
end

clearscreen hideturtle
setlabelheight 15
drawlunch [start]
stepdo [make "lunch fput "sandwich :lunch]
stepdo [make "lunch lput "apple :lunch]
stepdo [make "lunch fput "juice :lunch]
stepdo [make "lunch lput "cookie :lunch]
stepdo [make "lunch butfirst :lunch]
stepdo [make "lunch butlast :lunch]
stepdo [make "lunch lput "carrot :lunch]
print sentence [FIRST gives] first :lunch
print sentence [LAST gives] last :lunch
print sentence [ITEM 2 gives] item 2 :lunch
print sentence [COUNT gives] count :lunch
